Answer: If I have understood your question properly, you should just be able to apply a simple planar rotation, ie: $$\begin{bmatrix}
Cos(\theta) &-Sin(\theta)) \\ 
Sin (\theta)&Cos(\theta)) 
\end{bmatrix}
*\begin{bmatrix}
x\\y 

\end{bmatrix}$$
where * denotes matrix multiplication, and $\theta$ is the angle you want to rotate by. This will rotate the point (x,y) along a circle centered at the origin. 
